{
  "resourceType": "Questionnaire",
  "id": "child-registration",
  "url": "https://medplum.player.ohs.dev/fhir/Questionnaire/child-registration",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "name": "ChildRegistration",
  "title": "Register child",
  "status": "active",
  "date": "2026-09-21",
  "subjectType": [
    "Patient"
  ],
  "_comment": [
    "Registers one child and the caregiver who brings them, in a single SDC template extraction.",
    "There is no ID pool: the child's business identifier IS the allocated FHIR UUID, so two",
    "devices registering offline can never collide on a number.",
    "caregiver card reads, and which can be referenced and updated on its own) and inline as",
    "Patient.contact (which travels with the child record wherever it goes). Both come from the",
    "same answers, so they cannot disagree.",
    "The caregiver is written TWICE on purpose, which the spec explicitly allows ('Some individuals",
    "may serve as both a Patient's Contact and a Related Person'): a standalone RelatedPerson, which",
    "the profile's caregiver card reads and which other resources can reference, and inline as",
    "Patient.contact, which travels with the child record wherever it goes. The two are tied together",
    "by the standard patient-relatedPerson extension so a reader knows they are ONE person rather",
    "than two contacts who happen to share a name.",
    "managingOrganization records the facility as FHIR data. It is NOT what scopes access --",
    "Medplum stamps meta.account from the signed-in practitioner's AccessPolicy compartment, which",
    "the client cannot even represent. The two are independent, and only the server's one is",
    "enforced.",
    "__PRACTITIONER_ID__ and __ORGANIZATION_ID__ are substituted at launch. If either is unknown,",
    "QuestionnaireService DROPS the element rather than writing a dangling reference."
  ],
  "extension": [
    {
      "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/sdc/StructureDefinition/sdc-questionnaire-extractAllocateId",
      "valueString": "childId"
    },
    {
      "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/sdc/StructureDefinition/sdc-questionnaire-extractAllocateId",
      "valueString": "caregiverId"
